	(text "cell 6 sits 21-25V above ground, and its voltage is a 2.5V - 4.2V difference on that. \nThis circuit removes common-mode voltage mechanically rather than cancelling it. ==> differential sensing\n\nWe cannot put 21.6V on a 3.3V pin which destroys the pin. \nAnd we cannot measure the two ends separately and subtract,\nbecause we'd be finding a 3.6V answer by subtracting two ~20V readings, \nand all the error from both lands on that small difference.\n\nADG1408 Datasheet: https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/ADG1408_1409.pdf\n1. switches connect a cap across cell 6 only, and charges it to 3.6V\n2. switches disconnect both ends from the stack. cap now floats, holding 3.6V touching nothing\n3. switches connect cap's bottom to 0V and its top to ADC ==> ADC reads 3.6V\n\nCap only stores charge; the voltage across it doesn't depend on where it was.\n18V ground is not canceled but physically connected.\n\nRepeat this for cells 1 through 6, one at a time.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 32.385 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3f339b2b-f79b-4a19-8ae9-16b21f4cc738")
	)
	(text "1k sized by FAULT protection,\nso mishap can't destroy muxes\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 87.884 69.85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "47160caa-79b8-4d8c-956f-06bc873adaa0")
	)
